      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for immediate-release metformin, which is 2,550 mg/day (usually given as 850 mg three times daily). A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max labeled dose)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, such as 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO** at a different frequency\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you want, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
